A||N||2||bhop||tail lights, brake lights and headlight problem||||9||
Z||000000||bhop||12-11-2001||06:46 PM||||I have diconnected C500 and now when I step on the brake the radio clock does not go out. But when I turn on the headlights the radio clock goes out. I still do not have any lights in the back. Does anyone know where the engine blower relay is located? <BR>Any ideas from you Fiero Buffs would be appreciated.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Bhop||||reg||9
Z||000001||JohnF||12-11-2001||07:05 PM||||<BR>geeeeeez!  I see lots of problems in this one!<P>First, check your battery voltage. Make sure that you have 13.5+ volts output at the alternator (and on your gauge).  The ECM has to have good voltage or you get all kinds of weird stuff everywhere (especially, including the radio).<P>Second, check your fuses.  They could be faulty.<P>Check your ENGINE light output for faults.<P>Now, let us know what you find out.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||10
Z||000002||GTDude||12-11-2001||08:56 PM||||Do you mean the engine blower relay...or the coolant fan relay....or the a/c blower relay?  You said engine blower relay so I'll tell you where that is first.  It is located on the V6 model in the trunk (behind the engine) on the right hand side very close to the blower.  If you mean the a/c blower relay, it's located in the front compartment on the "firewall" about 6" to the left of the blower motor.  If you mean the coolant fan relay...it's located at the front right side of the front compartment.  Three relays are side by side...it is the one on the far left, standing looking at the underside of the hood.  Wire colors are red, black/red, brown/white and dark green/white.<P>I have repair manuals on all fieros, let me know if you need help with the lights and stuff.<P>GTDude<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||3
